==English==

===Etymology===
From stem of {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|expenditus}}, irregular perfect passive participle of {{m|la|expendo||I weigh, I pay out}}, {{suffix||ure|gloss2=process or result|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-expenditure.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} Act of [[expending]] or [[paying]] out.
# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} The [[amount]] [[expended]]; [[expense]]; outlay.
#: ''The '''expenditure''' of time, money, and political capital on this project has been excessive.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|act of expending}}
* {{sense|amount expended}} {{l|en|disbursement}}, {{l|en|expense}}, {{l|en|payment}}, {{l|en|cost}}, {{l|en|charge}}, {{l|en|outlay}}

